\name{cellucid_history_jump}
\alias{cellucid_history_jump}
\title{Show a step}
\usage{
cellucid_history_jump(viewer, at, bookmark, step)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{at}{A time (milliseconds since 1970): show the last step at or before it on the branch shown. A number. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{bookmark}{A bookmark's name (any case): show the step it marks. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{step}{A step of the tracker in use, by its id (history_get lists the steps). Text. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{head} (The step shown now).
}
\description{
Show the state after any step of the tracker in use, on any branch, as clicking it in the timeline does; nothing is undone or lost. Name exactly one of step, bookmark or at.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.jump} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_jump(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
